1. Install the Gutenberg plugin:

To develop custom blocks, you need to have the Gutenberg plugin installed. You can either install it from the WordPress dashboard or download it from the official WordPress repository and install it manually.

2. Create a new plugin:

Create a new folder in the `wp-content/plugins` directory of your WordPress installation, and inside that folder, create a PHP file with a descriptive name, such as `custom-block.php`.

3. Register the block:

Open the PHP file you created in step 2, and add the following code to register your custom block:

```php
<?php
/**
 * Plugin Name: Custom Block
 * Description: A custom block with a heading, paragraph, and image.
 * Version: 1.0.0
 * Author: Your Name
 * Author URI: https://yourwebsite.com
 * Text Domain: custom-block
 */

function create_custom_block() {
    register_block_type( 'custom-block/custom-block', array(
        'editor_style' => 'editor-styles.css',
        'style'        => 'style.css',
        'script'       => 'script.js',
    ) );
}
add_action( 'init', 'create_custom_block' );
```

Replace `Your Name` and `https://yourwebsite.com` with your own information.

4. Create the block template:

Create a new file named `template.php` in the same folder as your PHP file. This file will contain the HTML structure for your custom block.

```php
<?php
/**
 * Custom Block Template
 */
?>

<div class="custom-block">
    <div class="custom-block__content">
        <?php if ( has_block( 'core/paragraph' ) ) : ?>
            <div class="custom-block__paragraph">
                <?php the_block_content(); ?>
            </div>
        <?php endif; ?>

        <?php if ( has_block( 'core/heading' ) ) : ?>
            <div class="custom-block__heading">
                <?php the_block_content(); ?>
            </div>
        <?php endif; ?>

        <?php if ( has_block( 'core/image' ) ) : ?>
            <div class="custom-block__image">
                <?php the_block_content(); ?>
            </div>
        <?php endif; ?>
    </div>
</div>
```

5. Create the editor styles:

Create a new file named `editor-styles.css` in the same folder as your PHP file. This file will contain the CSS styles for your custom block in the block editor.

```css
